<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Bead nexus-p2m1x.26 (RDR-229 P3.6, item 7): a label names exactly one LIVE collection per tenant.

    catalog-052-1  idx_catalog_collections_live_label: a partial UNIQUE index on nexus.catalog_collections
                   (tenant_id, name) over the rows that are not superseded (superseded_by = ''). The name becomes the
                   label (item 7), and the one uniqueness rule it keeps is for addressing: two live collections of
                   one tenant may not answer to the same label, so a label in a command names one collection.
                   Labels in different tenants are independent.

                   Until P4.1 the name is still the primary key (catalog_collections_pk on (tenant_id, name),
                   catalog-001-5), so a superseded row, including one a past rename left, keeps its name taken, and
                   no existing row can break this index: it is built over a set the key already makes unique. The
                   index starts to matter at P4.1, when the key moves to the id and a tombstone releases its label. P4.1
                   re-creates this index over superseded_by_id IS NULL in the same changeset as the key swap, because
                   dropping superseded_by drops an index whose predicate names it (T2 229-research-45).

                   An additive CREATE UNIQUE INDEX over rows the primary key already keeps unique: no row is touched
                   and none can fail it, so there is no DATA EFFECT line. A plain CREATE INDEX (not CONCURRENTLY),
                   because Liquibase runs a changeset in a transaction; the table holds one row per collection,
                   so the build is brief.

                   NO WEDGE (as collections-001-2, the nexus-lgdel.l1 directive). The build takes SHARE on the registry,
                   which waits behind every open writer, so it runs under SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s'; and the
                   changeset is failOnError="false". A build that cannot get its lock in time, or that the migration role
                   may not run (it no longer owns the table), fails, is rolled back and logged, writes NO
                   DATABASECHANGELOG row, and the walk goes on; the next boot retries it. Skipping it costs nothing
                   until P4.1, since the primary key keeps the same rows unique (CollectionTupleUniqueIndexLiquibaseTest
                   holds a writer for a whole walk and moves the table's owner, and requires the walk to finish).

    The label rule itself (non-empty, valid UTF-8, no control character, at most 255 bytes, not the minted form) is
    the engine's CollectionLabel.validateUserLabel, called on the registration and rename routes, not a constraint
    here.

    ROLLBACK drops the index.

    Placed after catalog-050-note-uri-residue-owner-read.xml (the tail when this landed) and before the
    grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block (the established late-append convention, D0.1).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="catalog-052-1" author="nexus-p2m1x.26" failOnError="false">
        <comment>Creates idx_catalog_collections_live_label, a partial UNIQUE index on nexus.catalog_collections (tenant_id, name) WHERE superseded_by = '' (RDR-229 P3.6: a label names one live collection per tenant). Additive, over rows the (tenant_id, name) primary key already keeps unique, so no existing row can fail it and none is touched.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_catalog_collections_live_label
    ON nexus.catalog_collections (tenant_id, name)
    WHERE superseded_by = '';
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
                DROP INDEX IF EXISTS nexus.idx_catalog_collections_live_label;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
